+# Rolling-Wave Planning: Approved Local Clarification
+
+Status: Approved local methodology clarification
+project: t3-code-sample
+Date: 2026-10-27
+Owner: Chuck Russell
+Authority: docs/methodology/guides/gates.md and docs/methodology/guides/phase-loop.md
+Produced by: Codex under Chuck Russell's approved request
+Produced on: 2026-10-27
+Produced with: human-agent collaboration
+Agent identity: GPT-6.1 Sol via T3 Code
+Derived from: installed GenDev 1.0.2 phase-loop guidance and the approved issue 3 scope
+
+## Decision and scope
+
+Chuck Russell approved the described issue 3 changes with "Approve - make those
+changes" on 2026-10-27.
+
+Align the phase-planning skill and phase-loop guide on advance drafting versus
+formal acceptance. The project-wide phase plan describes the full phase
+structure, requirement ownership, dependencies, coverage contract, and
+integration criteria. Phase build plans may be drafted ahead to clarify scope
+and non-goals. Detailed tactical plans and construction directives are developed
+and finalized just before their phase, informed by prior-phase learnings.
+
+## Acceptance boundary
+
+Advance drafts remain Draft. They do not enter, close, or advance a checkpoint,
+issue a future-phase build prompt, authorize code generation, or establish that
+future work has been executed or accepted.
+
+Formal acceptance still requires the applicable checkpoint prerequisites,
+required approval, and pinned upstream authority. The phase sequence, G5.0 and
+G5.<id>.1 through G5.<id>.4 checkpoint definitions, phase-exit conditions, and
+approval requirements retain their existing meaning. The normative gate
+definitions remain unchanged. Phase N+1's tactical plan cites phase N's
+learnings; the first phase records N/A.
+
+## Installation provenance and limits
+
+This is a local clarification to installed GenDev 1.0.2, not a new upstream
+release. The constitution, normative gate definitions, source repository, and
+earlier approved clarifications are unchanged.
+
+The installation record retains the original source commit. This amendment's
+entry preserves each baseline file's original source hash, its previous
+effective hash, and its new effective hash. The planning skill already includes
+issue 2's amendment; this change builds on it rather than replacing that history.
+Integrity checks use the approved effective content. Reconcile or reapply local
+clarifications when upgrading the baseline.
+
+This changes planning guidance and its documentation/provenance only. It does
+not draft or approve product scope, change task state, authorize product code,
+or advance the pending G1 gate.
